      "why": "pipelined_m had 0 feasible in 50 evals, likely because the default search hit m values or parameter combos that broke the batch-latency or throughput bound. However, pipelined_m with small m (2-4) can reduce register count vs full pipelined while still giving 1 result/cycle. The sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.5 us constraint is tight: 32 requests must complete within 0.5 us of the tick. With 1 result/cycle, 32 cycles must fit in 0.5 us, requiring Fmax >= 64 MHz. pipelined_m with m=2-4 has fewer pipeline registers than full pipelined, potentially allowing higher Fmax at similar area. Worth a focused search with m constrained to 2-4 to avoid the latency penalty of large m."
