  "rationale": "The fleet facts show pipelined is the only family producing feasible designs (14 feasible, best area 41388 um2), while iterative and unrolled_k have 0 feasible (they cannot meet the 32 req/us throughput since they produce <1 result/cycle). pipelined_m also had 0 feasible in 50 evals, but this may be due to the search hitting unfavorable m values or parameter corners. I allocate 60% to pipelined (proven feasible, refine the Pareto front) and 40% to pipelined_m (focused search on small m=2-4 to see if it can beat pipelined on area while meeting the tight 0.5 us batch latency). Both families are constrained to data_width 14-18 and n_iter 12-18, which is the region where max_abs_err <= 2^-12 is achievable. angle_guard and frac_guard are kept small (0-2) to minimize area while preserving accuracy. The sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.5 us constraint is the binding system constraint: 32 results in 0.5 us requires Fmax >= 64 MHz with 1 result/cycle, so Fmax must be high enough. The area objective pushes toward minimal data_width and n_iter that still meet accuracy, while the accuracy_bits objective (HV ref 12) rewards designs that exceed the 12-bit accuracy floor."
