  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "The exploration has successfully identified a feasible Pareto front that satisfies all system and accuracy constraints. The minimum area design is a `pipelined_m` unit with `m=2`, `data_width=17`, and `n_iter=14`, achieving an area of 29,151 um^2 and 12.3 bits of accuracy (max error 2^-12.26), which meets the 2^-12 requirement. The `sys_p99_batch_us` constraint (<= 0.5 us) is met by the best designs (best seen 0.288 us), and throughput is well above the 32 MSPS requirement. Since this is the final round and the front covers the trade-off space from 29k to 56k um^2 with accuracy up to 14.7 bits, further exploration is unnecessary. The selection rule (min area) will pick the 29,151 um^2 design."
